# Meshtastic Scheduled Announcer

A lightweight Python-based Meshtastic automation script designed to run from Linux cron jobs and periodically announce node and mesh statistics to a Meshtastic channel.

This project was inspired by MeshMonitor automation concepts but is intentionally designed as a standalone script using the native Meshtastic Python API and TCP connectivity.

---

## Features

- TCP connection to a Meshtastic node
- Configurable message templates
- Dynamic token replacement
- Scheduled execution via cron
- Optional state-change detection
- Rotating log files
- Dry-run testing mode
- User-defined custom tokens
- Mesh statistics reporting
- Python 3.10+ compatible
- Future-ready token architecture

