# Configuration

## config.yaml

```yaml
meshtastic:
  host: 192.168.1.10
  channel_index: 0

announce:
  enabled: true
  send_only_on_change: false

  template: |
    {LONG_NAME} / {NODE_ROLE}
    Nodes {NODE_COUNT} ({DIRECT_COUNT} direct; {ONE_HOP_COUNT}/{TWO_HOP_COUNT}/{THREE_PLUS_HOP_COUNT} hops)
    Util {CHANNEL_UTIL}% TX {AIRTX}%
    Best {TOP_NEIGHBOR} {BEST_SNR}dB
    {FIRMWARE} / {HW_MODEL}
    {POSITION}
    {TIME}

custom:
  SITE_NAME: "Nebuchadnezzar"
  NODE_ROLE: "North Mesh Gateway"

logging:
  file: /var/log/meshtastic-announcer.log

state_file: /opt/meshtastic-announcer/state.json

weather:
  enabled: false

units: imperial
```

Meshtastic text payloads are limited to 233 UTF-8 bytes. The dry run reports the
rendered payload size; the script rejects oversized messages before transmitting.

Set `units` to `metric` (the default) or `imperial`. This controls
`{TEMPERATURE}` (°C / °F), `{GROUND_SPEED}` (km/h / mph), and `{ALTITUDE}`
(m / ft). `{BAROMETRIC_PRESSURE}` always remains in hPa. Add the matching unit
labels to the template, for example `{TEMPERATURE}°F` when using imperial.

## Multiple Nodes and Channels

To announce from multiple nodes, configure `targets` under `meshtastic`. Each
target connects to its own node, reads that node's metrics, renders its own
announcement, and sends it to each listed channel index:

```yaml
meshtastic:
  targets:
    - host: 192.168.1.10
      channel_indices: [0, 2]
      request_environment_metrics: true
    - host: 192.168.1.11
      channel_indices: [1]
```

Each host must appear only once and each target must have at least one channel
index. The state-change check is tracked independently for each node and
channel. `--dry-run` displays the generated message for every target without
sending or updating state.

Set `request_environment_metrics: true` for a target with an environmental
sensor to request fresh telemetry when temperature or barometric pressure is
not already cached. This sends a Meshtastic telemetry request and waits for a
response; if the request fails, cached values are used and missing tags remain
`N/A`. Dry runs never send telemetry requests. For single-node configuration,
set `meshtastic.request_environment_metrics: true`.

When `targets` is omitted, the existing `meshtastic.host` and
`meshtastic.channel_index` settings continue to configure a single node and
channel.

