# Running

## Normal Execution

```bash
python3 announce.py
```

---

## Dry Run

Generate the message without transmitting.

```bash
python3 announce.py --dry-run
```

Example:

```text
--- Generated Message ---

📡 Nebuchadnezzar

Node: Tampa-North
Role: North Mesh Gateway

Nodes Seen: 58
Direct Nodes: 12

Updated: 2026-11-01 09:30:00
```

---

## Force Transmission

Send regardless of change detection.

```bash
python3 announce.py --force
```

## TCP Send Delay

After calling the Meshtastic Python API to send an announcement, the script
keeps that node's TCP connection open for 2 seconds after each channel send.
This gives the node time to process each outgoing message before disconnecting.
With multiple targets or channels, allow roughly 2 seconds per channel send,
plus connection and metrics time, when setting an external command timeout.
Dry runs also keep each node connection open for 2 seconds before closing it,
so the Meshtastic library's background connection activity can finish cleanly.

The `Announcement sent` log entry means the local send call returned; it does
not confirm that the message was transmitted over the air or received by other
nodes.

